{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers","id":1303383,"title":"What are Iconic Fae Powers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-07T12:35:13-07:00","id":1303383,"title":"What are Iconic Fae Powers?","content":"When you think of Noble Raksha, what capabilities do you think of? If you were going to play one, what powers would you insist upon having? What are things which, if they didn\u2019t have, would make them feel wrong?<br /> <br /> There\u2019s no wrong answer and people are entitled to their opinions, so please no disagreements. It\u2019s also ok to say things like \u201cthat one charm that let them be perfect\u201d or \u201cthe ability to eat background emotion\u201d or whatever. You don\u2019t have to go look up specific names from previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T12:45:28-07:00","id":1303385,"title":"","content":"Creating an army of hobgoblins and monsters<br /> <br /> Being so unearthly beautiful or terrifying that mortal hearts are enslaved or stopped<br /> <br /> Bringing nightmares or dreams into creation <br /> <br /> Trolling the shit out of the Exalted","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T13:21:38-07:00","id":1303392,"title":"","content":"Forcing others to play along with their chosen roles, even if they should <i>know</i> they're nonsense.<br /> <br /> Redefining the nature of a conflict, such that participants must use different traits; demand everyone use combat Abilities for rolls in a tense negotiation, or replace someone's Strength rating with their Manipulation.<br /> <br /> Turn personal symbolism into literal fact; manifest a larger-than-life personality as Legendary Size, or sever limbs with a sharp tongue.<br /> <br /> Be in multiple places at once.<br /> <br /> Lie so convincingly that inanimate objects believe them.<br /> <br /> Make someone love or hate them so much that they just become an aspect of the raksha.<br /> <br /> Live to fight another day.<br /> <br /> Live happily ever after, at everyone else's expense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T13:43:23-07:00","id":1303399,"title":"","content":"Suck out people's emotions.<br /> <br /> Illusions and fantasy.<br /> <br /> Manipulate emotions, especially love and terror.<br /> <br /> Wield bizarre artefacts and ride monsters.<br /> <br /> Create hobgoblins.<br /> <br /> Doing things with dreams or nightmares, including making them real.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T14:26:54-07:00","id":1303409,"title":"","content":"Catch people within narratives forcing them to play a role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T15:38:56-07:00","id":1303419,"title":"","content":"Not comprehending all this fuzz about death it\u2019s just a temporary means to an end is it not?<br /> <br /> Feeding on emotions and intimacies when snacking and eating souls when feasting.<br /> <br /> Wielding Behemoths and weird artifacts.<br /> <br /> Conjuring equipment like clothes, armour, weapons, armies of hobgoblins and weather phenomena or environments.<br /> <br /> Not being limited to humanoid forms and forming bodies out of elements, emotions or concepts.<br /> <br /> Being living stories that catch people and Exalted alike in their narratives.<br /> <br /> Beautiful and horrifying beyond comprehension, often at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T15:49:01-07:00","id":1303420,"title":"","content":"A feeling of effortlessness in their actions, regardless of actual proficiency. (I'm trying to put into words what I like about their naturally high dice pools other than just having those dice)<br /> <br /> A casual ability to enchant and ensnare (Through shaping, charms or Onieromancies.)<br /> <br /> A kind of off-kilter power set, where their magic isn't necessarily in the strength of their abilities, but in the sweeping and/or esoteric effects.<br /> <br /> In an OOC way, I also really really enjoyed creating Behemoths and Onieromancies with the 2e charmsets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1982-spacepup","name":"Spacepup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T16:43:31-07:00","id":1303430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers#post1303383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you think of Noble Raksha, what capabilities do you think of? If you were going to play one, what powers would you insist upon having? What are things which, if they didn\u2019t have, would make them feel wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Holden always said that they were supposed to be particularly, dangerously effective when they spoke to you, which I got, but never quite thought stood out.<br /> <br /> The question is difficult for me, and makes the prospect of them being playable seem more awkward than ever, because between Adeimantus and the references in Fangs at the Gate, it seems to me that there are no iconic raksha powers; there are powers iconic to <i>this</i> raksha, or to that one.<br /> <br /> That said, once I got a look at the former's full write-up (courtesy of yourself), the most intriguing thing to me was the manner in which he could empower himself by allowing others to define him. I suppose that could be seen as a power in common that is distinct and iconic; that they are hollow men, who can turn that into a source of strength by allowing environment and the perceptions of others to fill in the gaps.<br /> <br /> I'd drop the narrative stuff; I find it too limiting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T16:46:41-07:00","id":1303431,"title":"","content":"Inspiring intense emotions in humans, and then devouring those emotions to leave the victim feeling lost and utterly numb, desperate to feel that intensely again. To feel anything.<br /> <br /> Forging a beast which is less a creature and more an extension of your own being. Whoever successfully steals it from you and tames it claims a very personal power over you as well.<br /> <br /> In fact, forging a number of things from your own soul. An artifact of mighty magic. An oath that grants power in return for conditions. A spell fit to rival the powers of Celestial Exalted sorcerers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Relying on hordes and minions, but the approach needs to change. Powers to enhance command actions, distraction gambits, and benefits from receiving distraction gambits are all well and good, but I think there should be powers that encourage Fair Folk to send their minions to attack you even without the Raksha present to command them.<br /> <br /> Actually, powers that involve commanding their minions remotely.<br /> <br /> The Raksha should act like the final boss of a video game or movie; they deliberately send their hordes and sub-bosses after you to extend the story and make it more exciting when you finally do confront them.<br /> <br /> To whit, a Raksha should be capable of forging minions specifically to counter you. Shades and dark mirrors of yourself that twist your ideals and mock your weaknesses. Even if you overcome the challenge and grow from it, the raksha likewise learns a valuable lesson about you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like the Lunar Exalted, the Raksha need their own ability to play the part of Maleficent, transforming into a giant dragon to do battle with the heroic knight to wake the princess she has cursed to sleep forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T16:51:37-07:00","id":1303432,"title":"","content":"Unsurpassed ability to create environments which can be utterly bizarre and which grant them all sorts of homefield advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T18:43:58-07:00","id":1303448,"title":"","content":"For those who have played Raksha before, what do you enjoy about it? What did you find problematic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T00:32:01-07:00","id":1303484,"title":"","content":"Noble Raksha? Taking and consuming parts of their commoner subordinates more or less freely, both ephemeral and physically.<br /> I always thought having multiple assumptions to choose from was cool. Netesh the brigand of rosy lips? Never heard of em! I\u2019m flamebright Netesh, bearer of eleven sparks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T02:11:23-07:00","id":1303491,"title":"","content":"I always found the enemy in anime &quot;shakugan no shana&quot; to be a good inspiration for Rakshas, even more now in this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12370-lddm84","name":"LDDM84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T05:26:47-07:00","id":1303502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1303448#post1303448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who have played Raksha before</div> </div> </div> </div>Not played a Raksha but a Lunar with Fair Folk charms.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">what do you enjoy about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really enjoyed the freeform nature of wyld stunts.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did you find problematic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bedlam. It's a big part of why I've never played a fae, their limit equivilent is a personality inversion that can persist for years until it has inconvenienced the player (and by extension, the group)<b> repeatedly</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T10:16:46-07:00","id":1303553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1303448#post1303448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who have played Raksha before, what do you enjoy about it? What did you find problematic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven\u2019t played one, but I\u2019ve played with one and ST\u2019d for one and I have to say I found them very difficult to adjudicate and deal with. <br /> <br /> The problem that I see is that a lot of players get super into these really cool abstract ideas, like when you battle a Raksha everyone gets pulled into a world halfway between reality and their own dreams, and populated by monsters that are manifestations of their own personal nightmares. Unable to battle these creatures normally, because they are a part of you, overcoming them means letting go of your fears and letting it wash over you. Then once that\u2019s finished the dream world melts away, and the sylvan lord with it. <br /> <br /> So that\u2019s cool, but how the fuck do I make that a charm? And what happens when a PC uses it? <br /> <br /> Also other kind of odd effects like the ability to instantly create a grand palace out of glass, antlers and giant twisted bone, but it\u2019s only real to you if you empty your mind. Because you aren\u2019t creating it, it\u2019s always there with you, in your spirit. It just can\u2019t be seen because a mind cluttered by stray thoughts can not see through the physical world to that which permeates the soul, and can and feel what\u2019s really there.<br /> <br /> Which, again, how do I do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T10:27:26-07:00","id":1303557,"title":"","content":"I play alongside a Raksha PC, and I think the player enjoys being an ancient alien creature from beyond reality who laughs at the bizarrities of Creation. And also having enormous stats. And just generally being a wandering tricksy adventurer who causes chaos where he/she goes.<br /> <br /> But I think the lack of charm support is a bit annoying. Still, I think he just uses stuff based on 2nd ed charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T10:40:51-07:00","id":1303562,"title":"","content":"Raksha?<br /> Playing a character type, and must stay in character type. There may not be a &quot;real&quot; me under it all. <br /> Eating intimacies (defining to major, major to minor, minor to nothing).<br /> Installing and strengthening intimacies (so that my feast will be even better).<br /> Creating whatever I need (as long as my story supports it).<br /> Minions and mid-bosses at my disposal.<br /> Enmeshing people in my story, like flies in a web, because my story is all that gives me the will to continue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T13:14:48-07:00","id":1304300,"title":"","content":"Thinking about some descriptions of the powers of the Sword Empress, I think that the capabilities for Raksha nobles can end up being fairly diverse, but whatever they do, there's a shaping element to it. They don't merely attack, they throw strikes that blight and wither (or they make themselves superior dancing warriors through mystical self-examination). They don't train armies, they conjure them up. They don't build natural things, they craft fantastical materials via poetry and ritual. It's even in the manner in which they take influences from others, and probably how they influence in turn.<br /> <br /> I propose that tends to meld qualities together, often overlaying the direct with the abstract and artistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T13:32:29-07:00","id":1304306,"title":"","content":"Being mutable. They are beings created whole cloth with the ability to create, discard, and change aspects of themselves. These beings are then placed in a world where they can't, and the things done to them are lasting. Fun stuff.<br /> <br /> I feel like, while it had a tendency to get exaggerated and out of hand, the more &quot;narrative&quot; aspects of their consciousness almost seem like a byproduct of this condition. It did eventually do them a disservice though, especially one I fell in to whenever I convince an ST to let me play one. In order to make my case and fit into games I usually fell into that trap.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, yeah, big stats, warping the world around them. Shit like that.<br /> <br /> Pocket Behemoths, Pocket Dimensions, Glamours and Sorcery were also particularly fun.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T15:04:57-07:00","id":1304324,"title":"","content":"Mutability is tricky with Rakasha. They need to be at least somewhat mutable on account of their origins, but if they\u2019re too mutable they become boringly undefined and interchangeable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T16:03:10-07:00","id":1304332,"title":"","content":"Clothing yourself in the Five Elements is pretty iconic to earliest and rawest iteration of the Fair Folk in Exalted. If I were writing Fair Folk, I'd like to have a look at the early fiction Nobles that sprung from that presentation, and emulating the sort of abilities that they suggest.<br /> <br /> It may also be useful to ask &quot;What can they not do?&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would like to defend reality shaping wars and games among their own kind, in the Wyld, though perhaps look for a less complex way to implement this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T19:40:57-07:00","id":1304377,"title":"","content":"I had a sequence of occurrences that led me to imagining Raksi descending from her towers to personally examine and deal with a phenomenon of fruit contaminated by the Wyld in a manner meaning that, when you open it up, it had something weird and inedible inside of it. Maybe the discovery of that area that mutates things to have qualities of yellow stone, I don't know.<br /> <br /> Apart from reminding me of how I need to actually sit down to watch Annihilation, it put me in mind of the depicted Raksha nobles as conveying a kind of personification of this state of the Wyld; that for them, being that kind of weird amalgamation is their natural state, and something that they thrive in.<br /> <br /> Well, it might be said of a lot of things native to the Wyld, so the nobility might be distinguished by ones who particularly represent it with something regal and edifying, an air of sophistication.<br /> <br /> And now that I'm writing all of this, I'm thinking of some other things to draw from it; that where nobles have powers to mutate others, rather than being free form, it has the form of shaping in a manner to share their aesthetics (even when those are in a more spiritual or psychological manner); really, being like living, walking Wyld zones with intent (which might end up being an accurate description of them). Or the idea that the process for Raksha growth (not just within nobility, but possibly the development from commoner to noble if that's still a thing) consists of a process of increasingly elaborating on those amalgamations, internalizing things that they encounter and react to (especially when they resonate with and can connect to already existing traits) to create ever more range and complexity in power, and more sophisticated purpose. <br /> <br /> The power to extract oaths might be seen in terms of Raksha interactions consisting of a dedicated process of directing those amalgamations, directly internalising and personifying roles of liege and vassal.<br /> <br /> A lot of that does end up being in line with prior depictions of the Raksha, but personally I find conceptualising it in terms of an ongoing process of characteristically Wyld mutation to make it a bit more visceral and compelling, and to help make more sense of what their powers might be and how they develop.<br /> <br /> But I'm also not seeing it as wholly divorced from narrative conceits, rather... externalising that from themselves a bit. I'm being driven by things I read when I took a look back at Masters of Jade recently; the idea of Guild members spreading narratives intended to alter local fae into more easily dealt with forms. In that approach, it makes narrative less of a thing inherent to the Raksha themselves, and more into something of Creation that especially beguiles and can be made to serve them. Narrative both in the sense of storytelling, of devices to convey theme, imagery and an ongoing structure, and in the sense of conveying information in ways that shape perceptions towards particular agendas.<br /> <br /> In that sense, the reputation of the Fair Folk as expert liars might not be in the sense of effective understanding of what lies are believable to what people, but that their shaping magic can spread into their very words, and their intent to influence; they can effectively relate ideas to their native personal theme without it needing to properly make sense, and at stronger levels their voice ends up effectively shaping your mind towards whatever belief system is in line with their nature. It never quite gets into outright mind control because that's too direct; it at least has to be in the Raksha saying <i>something</i>, even if the thing doesn't particularly make sense.<br /> <br /> Hmm, now I'm recalling the experience of being in a dream, where you can feel as though you're very conscious of everything that is happening, but take it all at face value; I've had times of feeling very rational inside of the dream about things that were somewhere between quite unlikely to utterly ludicrous, without any sense of contradiction or recognition. I'm now finding that would be a compelling basis for depicting the experience of being deceived and manipulated by a more powerful Fair Folk noble.<br /> <br /> Heh, this is one of those posts that started off shorter, and kept growing as putting the words down got me thinking of more and more implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T20:58:56-07:00","id":1304391,"title":"","content":"I always liked the idea that Raksha are kind of fascinated and horrified by how doggedly humans pursue safety and comfort.<br /> <br /> Like Raksha can approximate being desirous of something. It's a solid motivation,but it's one of many. You COULD be a boundless hedonist, but you could just as easily be a grim ascetic or vengeance-driven determinator.<br /> <br /> So when they look into Creation and see that most people pursue and would prefer to be in stories of luxury and power? It's weird. Like why would you retire to be with your family when you could be a scorned beggar on the street?<br /> <br /> I think some Raksha would interpret this tendency from humans to be a form of gluttony. 'They don't want to see the full gamut of experience! All they want is to eat and live and be... happy?'. With that in mind, I interpret the flashier, more luxurious assumptions Raksha take on to be their best impression of human nature.<br /> <br /> Like &quot;This is what you want, right? All the money you could ever need and everyone loves you.&quot;.<br /> <br /> This also goes some way to explaining why Raksha further into creation tend towards this kind of Bon Vivant expression while the ones further out are often more alien and esoteric.<br /> <br /> TL: DRIthink Raksha that go among humans take on celebratory and luxurious forms because they don't understand what makes humans seek out security and comfort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T08:42:12-07:00","id":1304444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304332#post1304332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clothing yourself in the Five Elements is pretty iconic to earliest and rawest iteration of the Fair Folk in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clothing yourself in the primary element of your environment, but not just any element.<br /> <br /> Raksha aren't going to wear the earth unless they're based somewhere underground playing at being dwarves and cave trolls. It would definitely be interesting if a raksha has to establish a fairy castle underground, which acts sort of like a manse from which he can draw Earth Essence that allows him to use Earth elemental powers. Or maybe they do, in fact, need a manse or demense.<br /> <br /> Requiring this sort of connection to an environment lends itself to forest-dwelling fairies becoming Forest Elves, and desert-dwelling fairies becoming Fire Elves. It ties them to a location, and from that restriction, they gain power.<br /> <br /> So when you're dealing with an elemental raksha, you take caution. But you also know they have a vulnerability you can attack to deprive them of that power. You know they have a treasure you can steal from them for your own power - a demense or manse.<br /> <br /> Previous Editions already made raksha keenly interested in taking demesnes or manses to build their homes, so why not expand on that?<br /> <br /> <br /> It also makes it meaningful to a raksha's story when they exchange a body of fire for a body of water. Because perhaps they were driven away from their fire-aspected demense and they had to flee to a water-aspected demesne before they returned for revenge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T09:32:59-07:00","id":1304447,"title":"","content":"well if you ever want Earth Aspect Raska the answer for that would be the Jade Born though it's not quite the same. Or rather it is quite different. different themes and such, but that does seem to be the intention anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 04-12-2019, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T09:55:13-07:00","id":1304460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304447#post1304447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well if you ever want Earth Aspect Raska the answer for that would be the Jade Born though it's not quite the same. Or rather it is quite different. different themes and such, but that does seem to be the intention anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>But do you want to encounter a castle of Fire Elves in a forest, or Sky Elves underwater, or Wood Elves underground? It's ridiculous.<br /> <br /> The raksha should fit the milieu of their surroundings, or of the environment from which they are staging their invasion, like a Fire Lord invading an Earth Kingdom from his base in the islands of the Fire Nation.<br /> <br /> Elemental powers are superfluous to raksha. They can be forest elves even without having Wood magic, so they don't need a Wood-aspected demesne. But if they're fortunate enough to find and claim a Wood-aspected demesne or manse, odds are it will be in a forest, so they can become elves in a forest with wood magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T10:52:44-07:00","id":1304467,"title":"","content":"Raksha can carry their context with them. Whatever props, foils, and sets they need to express their who-they-are, they can carry it within them as gossamer and spin it in to illusory glamour, like an insect knitting a shelter together out of silk. If a raksha is a Lord Of The Manor, they bring the manor and its inhabitants with them in their body, and exhale them in to the world in a way that's just real enough that it's in everyone's interest to play along with the conceit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T11:45:53-07:00","id":1304477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304467#post1304467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raksha can carry their context with them. Whatever props, foils, and sets they need to express their who-they-are, they can carry it within them as gossamer and spin it in to illusory glamour, like an insect knitting a shelter together out of silk. If a raksha is a Lord Of The Manor, they bring the manor and its inhabitants with them in their body, and exhale them in to the world in a way that's just real enough that it's in everyone's interest to play along with the conceit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'll roll with that for a moment. How much elemental power should that allow?<br /> <br /> If a Raksha could create a domain of ice and cold in the deep South, should she be able to summon blasts of ice and cold outside of that domain, or within the domain, or is her domain just an environmental hazard to anyone who enters it?<br /> <br /> And how easily should she be able to shed ice and cold from her story, to adopt a different elemental aspect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T11:57:58-07:00","id":1304479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304477#post1304477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I'll roll with that for a moment. How much elemental power should that allow?<br /> <br /> If a Raksha could create a domain of ice and cold in the deep South, should she be able to summon blasts of ice and cold outside of that domain, or within the domain, or is her domain just an environmental hazard to anyone who enters it?<br /> <br /> And how easily should she be able to shed ice and cold from her story, to adopt a different elemental aspect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Creating a domain of ice and snow in the South? That's a lot of power, because she's trying to get you to buy into a rather unbelievable story. She could still pull it off though.<br /> Outside that domain she would be limited, because she doesn't have enough personal power to fully pull off the whole thing, but weapons and creatures of ice and cold...more than likely.<br /> Within the domain? She could make a super-cold environmental hazard if she wished, or do the icy blasts, or both.<br /> Shedding her story? She's had to invest a lot into selling the Ice Queen in the South story. I would say she's locked into it as her identity until she gets defeated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T12:37:58-07:00","id":1304485,"title":"","content":"I feel as though, by and large, Exalted is not a game that lends itself well to the premise of being powerful only within a limited domain, because of the range that characters and games can have.<br /> <br /> With raksha in particular, when so many of them are supposed to have a story about them coming to you? Why is the Spear Empress able to chase whole nations when this Ice Prince isn't? <br /> <br /> I suppose Adeimantus kind of evinces those limits, insofar as he brings his borders with him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T13:19:36-07:00","id":1304492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304477#post1304477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Raksha could create a domain of ice and cold in the deep South, should she be able to summon blasts of ice and cold outside of that domain, or within the domain, or is her domain just an environmental hazard to anyone who enters it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The domain of ice and cold is not real. this domain is 'where-ever the raksha is'. It's an illusory overlay across the world, like a backdrop flung up behind the stage to suggest ice and snow. There is no point in describing the Raksha as 'outside' this domain because they aren't. The domain is where they are. They carry their illusion with them.<br /> <br /> The domain is an environmental hazard insofar as it's the mechanism by which they attack people in their space. The domain is not a passive 'place' - it is a glamour-aura they forcefully exude and impose upon the reality around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T14:45:11-07:00","id":1304511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304492#post1304492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The domain of ice and cold is not real. this domain is 'where-ever the raksha is'. It's an illusory overlay across the world, like a backdrop flung up behind the stage to suggest ice and snow. There is no point in describing the Raksha as 'outside' this domain because they aren't. The domain is where they are. They carry their illusion with them.<br /> <br /> The domain is an environmental hazard insofar as it's the mechanism by which they attack people in their space. The domain is not a passive 'place' - it is a glamour-aura they forcefully exude and impose upon the reality around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So would you say that a &quot;Wyld Storm&quot; is just a powerful raksha noble whose presence is felt even if people never see them, and so they only experience the changes wrought and left behind around it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T15:24:52-07:00","id":1304521,"title":"","content":"To me it seems like some of this swings back to earlier questions about how &quot;mutable&quot; Nobles should be. <br /> <br /> On a game level, partly this is going to be limited by the practicalities of player niche and role protection. <br /> <br /> On a narrative level, limits to how mutable characters create compelling stories (how much consistency of character do you need? how much does mutability serve the expression of character rather than negate it?).<br /> <br /> On a thematic level, the Nobles to me seem to have a dual role of wanting and fearing mutability; they are not quite the creatures of the Deep Wyld that they may have once been, and part of their themes *is* having shape thrust (oppressively) upon them by Creation. So how much does this justify that the lands they cross as they the enter the threshold into Creation become a defining immutable part of them?<br /> <br /> (This is probably getting off piste, but I do wonder how seriously you have to take, to some degree, in designing the Fair Folk, the internal mythology and bitterness of having hated shape thrust upon you, and striking out in bitterness against the shaped world. For players playing the Fair Folk, conventional Fair Folk as enemies of Creation, getting inside the headspace that Creation is a sort of violence on them could make them more compelling to play than simply shallow monsters? Those seem like they should be playable (a crusader of Balor as more than an empty manipulation and dramatic role, &quot;told by an idiot, full of sound and fury, signifying nothing&quot;). For all that I'd like Fair Folk as also unconventional allies of the Exalted to have a bit more fleshing out, along the lines I think hinted at in the early 1e material.)<br /> <br /> As another aside, having a quick look at Exalted: The Fair Folk, I noticed a little description of the Nobles as &quot;a domineering class of overlords who use their command over magic and ability to shape reality to enforce their rule&quot;. I quite like the imagine that, within Fair Folk society, rather than being particularly beguiling as they are to mortals, or skillful in the use of power, they simply declare reality such that they are in power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T17:20:21-07:00","id":1304541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304521#post1304521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a thematic level, the Nobles to me seem to have a dual role of wanting and fearing mutability; they are not quite the creatures of the Deep Wyld that they may have once been, and part of their themes *is* having shape thrust (oppressively) upon them by Creation. So how much does this justify that the lands they cross as they the enter the threshold into Creation become a defining immutable part of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Third Edition core presents it well with the idea that the main form of Creation's offence is that it contrasts their own emptiness, but it's also attractive because it provides a means to fill that emptiness with what they perceive to be more elaborate and meaningful drama.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(This is probably getting off piste, but I do wonder how seriously you have to take, to some degree, in designing the Fair Folk, the internal mythology and bitterness of having hated shape thrust upon you, and striking out in bitterness against the shaped world. For players playing the Fair Folk, conventional Fair Folk as enemies of Creation, getting inside the headspace that Creation is a sort of violence on them could make them more compelling to play than simply shallow monsters? Those seem like they should be playable (a crusader of Balor as more than an empty manipulation and dramatic role, &quot;told by an idiot, full of sound and fury, signifying nothing&quot;). For all that I'd like Fair Folk as also unconventional allies of the Exalted to have a bit more fleshing out, along the lines I think hinted at in the early 1e material.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That does sound like a possibility that an effective telling of the Raksha milieu and inviting and accessible mechanics would provide for a very experimental group. Even for more aggregable Fair Folk, I could imagine playing up a bitterness about the fallen conditions of their race to be a source of tension, or at least grit to a character. I think that part of the appeal of having somebody in the group be fae are the players needing to cope with the fact that, every now and then, the Wyld member is going to punctuate their usual boisterous dramatics with something lying between weird and horrifying. The Raksha might deflect their criticisms a bit by pointing to anything morally dubious that they do.<br /> <br /> Or just pull a Garak with &quot;don't act as though you didn't expect me to go this route, if not want me around specifically for these skills&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As another aside, having a quick look at Exalted: The Fair Folk, I noticed a little description of the Nobles as &quot;a domineering class of overlords who use their command over magic and ability to shape reality to enforce their rule&quot;. I quite like the imagine that, within Fair Folk society, rather than being particularly beguiling as they are to mortals, or skillful in the use of power, they simply declare reality such that they are in power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see some of that, but I also find something compelling in the likes of Judge Nehemeth presiding over her court by enforcement of a bunch of elaborate ritual and arbitrary rules, so I'd want a reconciliation.<br /> <br /> Oh, also that idea from the errata of how exerting too much control over those beneath them can be harmful to nobles, as it makes their circumstances uniform and static.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T11:14:46-07:00","id":1304647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304485#post1304485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though, by and large, Exalted is not a game that lends itself well to the premise of being powerful only within a limited domain, because of the range that characters and games can have.<br /> <br /> With raksha in particular, when so many of them are supposed to have a story about them coming to you? Why is the Spear Empress able to chase whole nations when this Ice Prince isn't?<br /> <br /> I suppose Adeimantus kind of evinces those limits, insofar as he brings his borders with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about him, since I didn't pay for access to him yet.<br /> <br /> But my idea about Raksha needing to tap demesnes or manses for elemental power is not about limiting that power to those locations, but tying their vulnerability to those places. The Forest Elf King can take his magical Wood powers with him when he sets forth from his domain, and those powers are not more powerful within that domain.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea for the possibility of raksha using celestially-aspected demesnes to become solar, lunar, and sidereal elves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T13:10:19-07:00","id":1304682,"title":"","content":"I will admit that there\u2019s a part of me that is getting enamoured of the idea that Raksha charms basically just don\u2019t operate like those in Creation, being more about dictating situations instead of interacting with the rules.<br /> <br /> Like, they\u2019ll have charms that make people Obsessed or give other Flaws, but not any that leverage the social influence rules. Or they\u2019ll just declare that \u201cthis place is a castle now\u201d and so it is. Or that they\u2019re \u201cThe best at X\u201d and so they are.<br /> <br /> That seems like it could be hellish to balance and create issues with interacting with them in a fun way though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T13:36:40-07:00","id":1304688,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that Adeimantus is at the far end of the power scale and would probably have been considered an Unshaped in 2nd edition due to his unique relationship with the city of Beimeni-Ta letting him spread his influence like a virus. He's the main antagonist of my Dragon-Blooded game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T15:07:59-07:00","id":1304704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304688#post1304688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that Adeimantus is at the far end of the power scale</div> </div> </div> </div>I find something useful in metrics given in the Second Edition errata; nobles on the level of Adeimantus (i.e. Essence 5, possibly 4) number in about a couple hundred per the outer four Directions, although often surrounded by a coterie of commoners. The likes of Spear Empress Bhadri might be a tenth of those, at best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">would probably have been considered an Unshaped in 2nd edition due to his unique relationship with the city of Beimeni-Ta letting him spread his influence like a virus.</div> </div> </div> </div>This just makes me think about how prior Editions underserved the concept of Wyld breakthroughs. That being said, I believe that there were Assumption Charms that could allow a shaped raksha to personify themselves in a settlement or geographic feature that would have Wyld properties.<br /> <br /> But for how he spreads his own Wyld properties, I think it's important to disassociate him with old systems, because the important thing about Adeimantus is that the Wyld isn't coming from him. Not directly, at least; he gives people the insight and inspiration to achieve their dreams with greater efficiency and flamboyance, in return for which they build and sanctify a shrine to him, and <i>that's</i> why the Wyld happens. I think it's important to convey the idea that the Wyld also springs up from sets of behaviours or strange happenstances; look at how the cockatrice is born.<br /> <br /> Going by Fangs of the Gate, I read Beimani-Ta as basically being his iconic panoply, in the manner of Bhadri's soul-shredding shrike, or the magical looking-glass of Maja of the Starling Song; he's deeply entwined with it, but it's ultimately just an expression of the power of his own legend of being a custodian of utopia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T17:07:08-07:00","id":1304718,"title":"","content":"Beimeni-Ta isn't even intrinsic to Adeimantus; if you killed him, another raksha could take control of the parasite-city. The city seems to be something like a &quot;shaping weapon&quot;, possibly a Treasure (artifact-equivalent, with Evocations) or an Oneiromancy (spell-equivalent).<br /> <br /> <br /> Or maybe Beimeni-Ta is a new vision of how Raksha Freeholds can operate; independent of any physical location, within a pocket dimension, capable of establishing breakthroughs anywhere in Creation according to the Freehold's nature; even in multiple different cities simultaneously.<br /> <br /> So Baba-Yaga's chicken-legged house isn't her Freehold; her Freehold is Baba-Yaga's Forest, which can intersect with any forest in Creation where a mortal wanders alone at night, allowing her to appear and take them away, or for mortals to seek her out and try to bargain with her. Her chicken-legged house is just a feature of her Forest, represented as a creature or behemoth.<br /> <br /> The other world of <i>Coraline's</i> Other Mother can appear anywhere in a similar fashion, so that the Other Mother can try to lure children into her world from anywhere.<br /> <br /> Pennywise's domain connects to sewers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T17:24:43-07:00","id":1304721,"title":"","content":"I kind of like the idea of instead of Raksha turning the dream-eaten into mindless drones, consuming a subjects\u2019 other intimacies while building an intimacy to the Raksha, and when the subject is entirely eaten, they only have that single intimacy left leaving them a stock player in the Raksha\u2019s narrative defined solely by that role, even if it\u2019s an antagonistic one.<br /> <br /> So someone becoming increasingly obsessed with killing a particular Raksha could actually be in the process of being dream eaten, as the Raksha consumes all their other intimacies through that intimacy until they\u2019re left a 2-dimensional Ahab of the Raksha\u2019s story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-13-2019, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T17:30:08-07:00","id":1304724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304721#post1304721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of like the idea of instead of Raksha turning the dream-eaten into mindless drones, consuming a subjects other intimacies while building an intimacy to the Raksha, and when the subject is entirely eaten, they only have that single intimacy left leaving them a stock player in the Raksha\u2019s narrative defined solely by that role, even if it\u2019s an antagonistic one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can a Raksha consume an Intimacy they despise, oppose, or are indifferent to?<br /> <br /> Generally the Raksha have been presented as eating passions that align with their own. Which had always seemed \u201cscorched earth\u201d to me, in that it turns mortals into things which bore them, leading them to discard mortals almost immediately rather than feeding on them for prolonged periods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T17:31:44-07:00","id":1304725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304724#post1304724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Raksha consume an Intimacy they despise, oppose, or are indifferent to?<br /> <br /> Generally the Raksha have been presented as eating passions that align with their own. Which had always seemed \u201cscorched earth\u201d to me, in that it turns mortals into things which bore them, leading them to discard mortals almost immediately rather than feeding on them for prolonged periods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not saying this conforms wto past rules for them, I\u2019m saying I think it\u2019s more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T17:52:04-07:00","id":1304733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304725#post1304725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m not saying this conforms wto past rules for them, I\u2019m saying I think it\u2019s more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u2019t be opposed to future Raksha having the power to eat parts of people they don\u2019t care for in order to shape those people into something more interesting, with the consumption of those final interesting elements being a powerful harvest enjoyed only by Raksha in need of an immediate boost, or hedonists who have no care for regular retainers.<br /> <br /> Raksha living on mortal worship through the Cult background also makes sense. Cultivate and breathe in adoration and/or fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T17:56:04-07:00","id":1304735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304733#post1304733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn\u2019t be opposed to future Raksha having the power to eat parts of people they don\u2019t care for in order to shape those people into something more interesting, with the consumption of those final interesting elements being a powerful harvest enjoyed only by Raksha in need of an immediate boost, or hedonists who have no care for regular retainers.<br /> <br /> Raksha living on mortal worship through the Cult background also makes sense. Cultivate and breathe in adoration and/or fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>What i\u2019m imagining is not trimming people in customizable ways. It\u2019s feeding on Intimacies via an intimacy to reduce the person to a caricature who only exists in relation to the Raksha. The only customizable part would be determining (via the individual and the Raksha\u2019s actions) what that one remaining Defining intimacy to the Raksha would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T18:09:49-07:00","id":1304737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304718#post1304718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beimeni-Ta isn't even intrinsic to Adeimantus; if you killed him, another raksha could take control of the parasite-city.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Maja's mirror was taken and converted into an Artifact for Lunars.<br /> <br /> I feel as though nothing is really intrinsic to the Raksha nobles; it all has to be something that they appropriate in some manner, and hence can be claimed from them by cleverness or right of conquest or the proper social decorum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe Beimeni-Ta is a new vision of how Raksha Freeholds can operate</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that the city can function as both by virtue of it being a location in the Wyld and thus qualifying as the mutating domain of a noble, but wouldn't want it to be standardised, because I feel as though that detracts from the city's backstory and its significance to Adeimantus personally. I'll note that while the write-up says that a member of his court could rise to dominion with his removal, they might not have the same take on or application for it.<br /> <br /> But for the moment, I think it's important that Beimeni-Ta was a very spiritual, philosophical city that was appropriated by the Wyld, claimed by a Raksha who styled himself as a municipal authority and spreader of utopian ideals, and thus the city's qualities are the means by which he can spread that.<br /> <br /> For breakthroughs, the essential quality that I would want is people enacting something that spreads mutation of a kind characteristic to the commanding noble, and makes the whole place Wyld-like. For the likes of Adeimantus, that's people with a connection to his city building something in emulation to it, which mutates the surrounding urban landscape into it, and mutates the people into its ideal citizens. For somebody more in the style of the Erlking, it could be inducing people to ritualistically hunt beasts and work their way up to other people, mutating themselves into monstrous hunters and their targets into prey that are alternately pitiful or suitably fearsome, and soon those mutations start spreading to the landscape and converting it into iconic primeval forest, changing those who enter by way of requiring them to find a role in the hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Baba-Yaga's chicken-legged house isn't her Freehold; her Freehold is Baba-Yaga's Forest, which can intersect with any forest in Creation where a mortal wanders alone at night, allowing her to appear and take them away, or for mortals to seek her out and try to bargain with her. Her chicken-legged house is just a feature of her Forest, represented as a creature or behemoth.<br /> <br /> The other world of <i>Coraline's</i> Other Mother can appear anywhere in a similar fashion, so that the Other Mother can try to lure children into her world from anywhere.<br /> <br /> Pennywise's domain connects to sewers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of a property of Freeholds in particular being able to hook up to areas that have been given a bit of Wyld by the actions of ravagers does intrigue me, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T18:50:53-07:00","id":1304741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304737#post1304737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Maja's mirror was taken and converted into an Artifact for Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what your point is.<br /> <br /> There's nothing said about Maja's mirror that makes it out to be anything but mirror that was important to her, personally. Maybe it had powers, maybe it was a Treasure or an Oneiromancy, but that wouldn't make it a Freehold like Adeimantus's city appears to be. Not an invasive, parasitic disease upon the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel as though nothing is really intrinsic to the Raksha nobles; it all has to be something that they appropriate in some manner, and hence can be claimed from them by cleverness or right of conquest or the proper social decorum. </div> </div> </div>Adeimantus' special bane is particular to him; his successor could have a different bane as well as a different vision for what kind of place the city should be.<br /> <br /> Adeimantus' Charms are particular to him; an Eclipse couldn't learn his city-reshaping Charm if it were an Evocation of the city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T19:10:29-07:00","id":1304743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304741#post1304741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what your point is.<br /> <br /> There's nothing said about Maja's mirror that makes it out to be anything but mirror that was important to her, personally. Maybe it had powers, maybe it was a Treasure or an Oneiromancy, but that wouldn't make it a Freehold like Adeimantus's city appears to be. Not an invasive, parasitic disease upon the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a whole thing from reading Fangs at the Gate in which it read to me as though there was a consistent pattern to those nobles in the form of having an iconic panoply.<br /> <br /> Maja's legend was of a swordswoman who would examine her form in her personal looking-glass in order to eliminate flaws, ensuring that she would be a superlative fighter. To the extent that it might have been a mirror that had no particular intrinsic magic, I'm proposing that the mere fact of being important to a Raksha noble in terms of the passion that drives them <i>makes</i> it important.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing it in terms of those old Raksha Artifacts, because I think those are a level of complexity that they could do without.<br /> <br /> In any case, sure it's not precisely the same as Adeimantus' panoply, because they're two different nobles with distinct approaches, as all of them are. I'm just suggesting that, where the ones in Fangs have their iconic tools that are part of how they exert themselves against Creation, Adeimantus has his city, because he is all about imposing his city and the utopian ideal associated with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adeimantus' special bane is particular to him; his successor could have a different bane as well as a different vision for what kind of place the city should be.<br /> <br /> Adeimantus' Charms are particular to him; an Eclipse couldn't learn his city-reshaping Charm if it were an Evocation of the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>My whole thing is about suggesting that all of that power comes from an identity that did not form independently, but from incorporating the city into himself.<br /> <br /> The city was once a real city, until the Wyld claimed it. And here we have a noble whose powers and purpose are essentially focused on this city claimed from Creation.<br /> <br /> Adeimantus' bane is <i>distinct</i> to him, but when it's a bane of being vulnerable to attacks by people who can't read the history of a pre-existing city that has been etched into his skin?<br /> <br /> Was there an Adeimantus before the city? Is there an Adeimantus underneath everything that he outwardly expresses that is concerned with it? If it was lost while he still lived, who would he be without it?<br /> <br /> If every signifier of your identity, of your power, of your motivation to act, comes from something that was stolen from somebody else, then none of those things are intrinsic to you.<br /> <br /> I mean, at least when you're an alien angel composed of hunger and lies from beyond the moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T03:21:25-07:00","id":1304774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304704#post1304704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find something useful in metrics given in the Second Edition errata; nobles on the level of Adeimantus (i.e. Essence 5, possibly 4) number in about a couple hundred per the outer four Directions, although often surrounded by a coterie of commoners. The likes of Spear Empress Bhadri might be a tenth of those, at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't find those particularly useful anymore. Would it be a good thing for Fair Folk PCs to have essentially 50 First Age elders per direction?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T04:51:04-07:00","id":1304783,"title":"","content":"Thanks for directing my attention towards, Adeimantus as he is a nice piece of work - to say the obvious, hits some of the notes of The King In Yellow/Carcosa and Tl\u00f6n, Moorcock's idea of Tanelorn and those themes of possession and invasion and being overtaken by a mirror of yourself which are part of the Fair Folk (noted explicitly upthread in reference to Coroline and other such works).<br /> <br /> Re; Levi' s statement on Fair Folk Nobles' natures as appropriative, I think it's an idea worth considering. It seems like it has some value - but I do think we should see Fair Folk as being capable of elaboration and extension and change in what they &quot;take&quot;, and also of reproducing themselves an passing an &quot;identity&quot; on to &quot;children&quot; or &quot;creations&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'd also kind of repeat (sorry) my earlier comment, I'd emphasize they also partake of being what is them thrust upon them (by Creation and the all-out-war of strong things in the Wyld), and then made their own. Playing a Fair Folk probably allows you to access personal and existential horror of having an identity thrust upon you (or being forced to pull it together from others scraps and leavings in order to 'fight back').<br /> <br /> Even from the perspective that you're not of Creation, I would argue they're not only there to powerful, self possessed agents of predation, greed, theft to be worked upon others. Part of them is the horror of things that Creation has forced upon beings of another alien nature, through its hubris and the inclusive, expansive ambitions of their domains and rule held by the Powers That Be through history (the Primordials, the Gods, man), coming back to roost. So I'd not really be inclined to have *too* much agency in being born only to self defining hunger and made by what they choose to take by will alone.<br /> <br /> (At least, that's the argument I'd make! This possibly depends on your taste for World Of Darkness-ish &quot;You are the monster&quot; personal horror type exploration things in Exalted? Whether those even work well at all, etc..).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T06:09:59-07:00","id":1304793,"title":"","content":"When I compare Adeimantus to an Unshaped I mostly mean in terms of his narrative role.<br /> <br /> In 2nd edition a Shaped Raksha who was going for Custodian of the Perfect City would be encouraged to just arrive throw down an oneiromancy spell to go &quot;this is my perfect city&quot; and people need to spend a bunch of wp/suffer dice penalties to oppose this. While Adeimantus kind of waits for people to come to him (possibly helping knowledge of the city spread through diplomats) and when it reaches critical mass he arrives via a breakthrough in what could be considered act 3 of this story when its already too late for the people with a connection to Beimeni-Ta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T06:15:15-07:00","id":1304794,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304783#post1304783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Re; Levi' s statement on Fair Folk Nobles' natures as appropriative, I think it's an idea worth considering. It seems like it has some value - but I do think we should see Fair Folk as being capable of elaboration and extension and change in what they &quot;take&quot;, and also of reproducing themselves an passing an &quot;identity&quot; on to &quot;children&quot; or &quot;creations&quot;.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I completely agree with that.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As regards children, when I first read Adeimantus (preview version), one of the first places my mind went was to old Fair Folk Charms for sanctifying oaths by creating another Raksha to personify them. In those mechanics, it made the oath itself binding in a similar manner to the Eclipse, but the new noble made me consider the notion that such a binding should create a being whose starting nature is being the embodiment and enforcer of the oath, and they grow from there.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The prior Editions had another Charm to allow more direct creation of other fae, but I wonder if they shouldn't get anything so direct in Third Edition.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'd also kind of repeat (sorry) my earlier comment, I'd emphasize they also partake of being what is them thrust upon them (by Creation and the all-out-war of strong things in the Wyld), and then made their own. Playing a Fair Folk probably allows you to access personal and existential horror of having an identity thrust upon you (or being forced to pull it together from others scraps and leavings in order to 'fight back').</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also agree with this. A long time ago, I had a notion of a noble that became a lot more dangerous because of what they internalised from a Solar humiliating them with defeat and leaving them to die at the bottom of a ravine.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Even from the perspective that you're not of Creation, I would argue they're not only there to powerful, self possessed agents of predation, greed, theft to be worked upon others. Part of them is the horror of things that Creation has forced upon beings of another alien nature, through its hubris and the inclusive, expansive ambitions of their domains and rule held by the Powers That Be through history (the Primordials, the Gods, man), coming back to roost. So I'd not really be inclined to have *too* much agency in being born only to self defining hunger and made by what they choose to take by will alone.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">(At least, that's the argument I'd make! This possibly depends on your taste for World Of Darkness-ish &quot;You are the monster&quot; personal horror type exploration things in Exalted? Whether those even work well at all, etc..).</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Second Edition had a notion that Fair Folk could shape their own Intimacies at will, but those made by the Creation-born weren't subject to this power. I think the first step is one that shouldn't be present considering the higher importance of Intimacies in this Edition, but keeping some of the spirit of the second, and then expanding on it, feels like it has potential to me. That it represents the backstory element of Creation imposing things like time upon them in a manner that plays out in interpersonal stories.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304774#post1304774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't find those particularly useful anymore. Would it be a good thing for Fair Folk PCs to have essentially 50 First Age elders per direction?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, more like twenty at the very highest (more likely fewer for a given Direction). I think there's a bit more latitude to have a few more high Essence Raksha for reasons including that it might still be difficult for them to spend a lot of time away from the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Besides, how many gods have Essence 6 or higher in a given Direction? They're not the equivalents of First Age elders in either case because their powers are very different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T07:02:46-07:00","id":1304802,"title":"","content":"They've got more in common with the First Age elders because Fair Folk are a PC splat and gods are not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T08:33:47-07:00","id":1304812,"title":"","content":"Should beginner PC Raksha characters be balanced like Dragon-Blooded or Lunar Exalted?<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded find it much more difficult to defend themselves against multiple attackers, and virtually impossible to attack multiple times or multiple targets in a single round, because they are meant to work in teams to fight the kind of battles that Celestial Exalted warriors can solo.<br /> <br /> Should Raksha be at a similar level, with a greater assumption that they will be fighting with familiars or battle groups?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T09:46:17-07:00","id":1304823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304802#post1304802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've got more in common with the First Age elders because Fair Folk are a PC splat and gods are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to make a comment about how First Age elders are Essence 5 with a gimmick, but that's also causing me to revise my notion of how many Essence 5 nobles there are.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it raises the question about what kinds of PCs they're like, since there's a broad range, and Raksha in particular presumably still have some constraints with operating in Creation.<br /> <br /> Hmm, there's also the matter for how, for PCs, actually achieving Essence 6 is a matter of fiat, so what it does for a given group might be arbitrary.<br /> <br /> But what does that mean for my desires that they be capable of contesting Celestial Exalted...?<br /> <br /> I don't know, but I'm at least somewhat convinced that my foundation is shaky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T12:53:32-07:00","id":1306070,"title":"","content":"My own instinct is that, in straight combat, Exalted can become too powerful for Raksha to meaningfully oppose. However, a truly masterful high-end Raksha has a breadth of competencies that will complicate this. They can bend Creation to their defense with glamourous influence, throw up hosts of illusory facades to take the fall on their behalf, drown their opposition beneath legions of disposable phantasms, etc. If their body is made of Gossamer rather than a mutation they imposed on themselves, they can even punt their physical body aside and book it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304511#post1304511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would you say that a &quot;Wyld Storm&quot; is just a powerful raksha noble whose presence is felt even if people never see them, and so they only experience the changes wrought and left behind around it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. The metaphor is that Creation is land, and the Wyld, the sea. The Marches are the continental shelf, and the Deep Wyld the deep sea beyond them. In this metaphor, a Wyld Storm is the tide coming in, or a storm swamping the bay. Not all Wyld Storms carry a raksha with them, but an unshaped raksha - the old, monstrous chaos-gods who never sullied themselves with anything as pathetically fixed as *a material body* - can ride that tide inland and tear a tide-pool in to the beach on their way in and out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T13:49:36-07:00","id":1306080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1306070#post1306070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own instinct is that, in straight combat, Exalted can become too powerful for Raksha to meaningfully oppose. However, a truly masterful high-end Raksha has a breadth of competencies that will complicate this. They can bend Creation to their defense with glamourous influence, throw up hosts of illusory facades to take the fall on their behalf, drown their opposition beneath legions of disposable phantasms, etc. If their body is made of Gossamer rather than a mutation they imposed on themselves, they can even punt their physical body aside and book it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I probably wouldn't have ever had a problem with Raksha if the game had never included any that so much as fashioned themselves as sword-fighters.<br /> <br /> But it did, and now I wants it. You show me a comic in which Dace is about to clash with a powerful cataphract noble, I thinks you need to actually give it to me.<br /> <br /> Out of all prior Fair Folk Charms, the ones of the Sword have to have always been the most disappointing to me. You have background fiction and caste descriptions describe Warriors and their noble expansions as being decent at fighting, and then what did they get to actually fulfil it? Giving themselves mutations?<br /> <br /> Hmm... {looks back at the book} Hundred-Hand Style, Millipede Mind and Grace of the Infinite Revolving Spheres seem like something, and while I've too little familiarity with the First Edition system to fully assess their values I've heard some people suggest that they're somewhere between pretty decent and kind of broken, but they don't convey the most inviting variety.<br /> <br /> And yes, I know that the Sword Grace isn't strictly about literal fighting, but again, when it presents Raksha who are relatively straightforward fighters, it sets me in a mind of wanting to do <i>something</i> to realise that.<br /> <br /> I understand that one of the original conceptions of the Fair Folk (and something that Holden seemed to want to adhere to the spirit of in his errata) that their advantage was supposed to be in having distinctly high dice pools more than Charms to enhance actions in the way that the Exalted might get. I have a suspicion that this (in combination with things like improved multi-actions and benefits to splitting dice pools) was more impressive in First Edition, and even with the benefit of a pseudo-Execellency never quite displayed itself well in Second. But even within its original milieu, to me personally it just doesn't feel very sexy when compared to the strength of the Exalted being represented through the variety of their Charms.<br /> <br /> Between the manner of variety for Exalted Charms and the abandonment of generic Charms to give spirits (especially demons) things that actually live up to and represent their legends, I feel as though this Edition now more than any other is the one where that duel between Dace and Lan-Shoki Hahna can unfold in suitable fashion, rather than leaving me to imagine the cataphract needing to sprout wings and making his arms extra long.<br /> <br /> Or at the very least, present a decent and coherent, if simplified, Charm set that is compelling enough to kill off the image of one as a sword fighter (although I'm not sure where that leaves Maja).<br /> <br /> I'll note that my standard isn't concerned with straight combat as such. I'm not exactly asking for the Essence 5 Raksha to fight on equal terms with the Essence 5 Solar or Lunar (although making a decent show of it wouldn't be half bad), I just want them to have the right look. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">an unshaped raksha - the old, monstrous chaos-gods who never sullied themselves with anything as pathetically fixed as *a material body*</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, the prior developers seemed to be of a mind that unshaped Raksha weren't really a thing anymore, and I'm not sure if the current developers are particularly compelled by them either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T14:10:59-07:00","id":1306083,"title":"","content":"The Raksha PC in our game has always done fine in combat with Dexterity 7, Melee 7, Stamina 5, Strength 5, and a magic sword.<br /> <br /> But then, it's never actually fought a combat Exalt, just martial artists, monsters, mobs of soldiers, etc. I suspect you're right, that it'd be quite unable to cope with fancy combat charms and stuff. But those are some really fat stats, that don't require any mote expenditure...<br /> <br /> Still, I'd say the writers agree with you, considering the Cataphract in the Core book has some decent-ish combat charms.<br /> <br /> 16 dice (16 damage) for a withering attack, Soak 14, Parry 7. A charm for attacking a bunch of people with your withering attack, a really strong anti-armour charm, an onslaught negator, and an okay soak charm.<br /> <br /> It's pretty tasty really, as swords-creatures go. No Dawn Caste, but still significant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-19-2019, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T14:28:43-07:00","id":1306086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1306083#post1306083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Raksha PC in our game has always done fine in combat with Dexterity 7, Melee 7, Stamina 5, Strength 5, and a magic sword.<br /> <br /> But then, it's never actually fought a combat Exalt, just martial artists, monsters, mobs of soldiers, etc. I suspect you're right, that it'd be quite unable to cope with fancy combat charms and stuff. But those are some really fat stats, that don't require any mote expenditure...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to survive, I want to live.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T15:33:45-07:00","id":1306097,"title":"","content":"I guess the whole thing for me about Nobles and having high dice pools, but not much capability to push them up higher, always seemed like it would tend to move into Exalts just pushing their dice cap high to alpha strike the Noble, and then... that's the end of the fight. Which seems kind of dull, if I'm getting the picture of how it shakes out right? Exalted-Exalted fights seem more like, you're not gonna do that because your opponent will just counter it by pushing up his pool, while fae can't credibly make the counter threat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T16:00:47-07:00","id":1306102,"title":"","content":"In First Edition a Fair Folk Cataprchtoi (sp?) managed to fight the groups Dusk Caste Abyssal into a tie, both lost their last health level at the exact same initiative, the only thing that saved the Abyssal was that some of the damage inflicted during combat was bashing so she was merely unconsious while the Fae lay dead. True the Fae did not fight fairly and used any advantage possible but still the fight was epic and will be remembered. The high dicepools of the Fae and the ability to divide those big pools efficiently was the key in direct round to round combat because it was bleeding way less motes than the Abyssal was.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1304812#post1304812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should beginner PC Raksha characters be balanced like Dragon-Blooded or Lunar Exalted?<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded find it much more difficult to defend themselves against multiple attackers, and virtually impossible to attack multiple times or multiple targets in a single round, because they are meant to work in teams to fight the kind of battles that Celestial Exalted warriors can solo.<br /> <br /> Should Raksha be at a similar level, with a greater assumption that they will be fighting with familiars or battle groups?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I think they should land somewhere in between. The Fair Folk should be able to fight multiple combatants at once through impossible wide attacks, multiplying themselves and/or summoning illusory soldiers that are more real than they at first seem. Armies of the Wyld were invading quite efficiently until the Empress did her thing so I\u2019d say they should be, the Nobles that is, perhaps slightly above or at the least same level as Dragon-Bloods but generally slightly less powerful than individual Lunar. But then again I think they should have Charms and mechanics that make possible the kinda twisted literal thinking that give them a fighting chance on even the Celestial Exalted. <br /> <br /> The Master Swordsman Noble should due to high stats be able to somewhat offer a challenge to a celestial and have Charms that allow it to bend the rules just so in it\u2019s favour that they can stand a chance in winning but only by playing unfairly, twisting the environment, summoning hazards, illusory copies of themselves, fake deaths (but what is death but an illusion for those of the Wyld?) and one that worlds a bow should have ability to fire arrows further than should be possible by bending the rules of distance or to fire a single arrow that kills a whole unit of soldiers by causing the wound to spread amongst mortals, etc.<br /> <br /> So impressive stats and the ability to bend and break the rules of reality to turn the tables on their enemies.<br /> <br /> And sometimes it should be possible that they turn their loss into victory, either through something like the false death or something more sinister like having been bestet and surrendering to their enemy could give them the opportunity to forge intimacies that tie their victor to them in a sudden reversal of the situation.<br /> <br /> As a side note my combat based Dawn Caste during our last 3rd edition game pretty nearly lost against a Fair Folk, I had considerable trouble in causing any significant withering damage to gain initiative against it, and I had fought the Living Tower into a standstill earlier so to have more trouble with this one was a surprise to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T23:59:31-07:00","id":1306191,"title":"","content":"I will say that I think Raksha, from the way they are portrayed in the fiction, should be hella scary to everyone. Including Solar exalted.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, not even the likes of Spear-Empress Bhadri should just be able to win forever against everyone.<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m not sure where the balance point is. I also feel like leaning too hard on anti-fae tech makes things disappointing. I mean, sure anti-fae charms and stuff should help, obviously, but if you can\u2019t so much as touch the Fae without said charms (or if the fae become chumps if you have the charms) things get problematic.<br /> <br /> It gets even more difficult if you want to include the whole \u201cclever mortals defeat powerful Raksha\u201d thing, because, while it can happen, stat comparisons suggest that it should be hella rare if the Fae can take on a Solar.<br /> <br /> So.... it\u2019s difficult to pin down any kind of rough guide for what power level the Fae should have, even, because of all these competing requirements. \u201cThey should be strong enough to challenge a Solar, but weak to mortal Thaumaturgy.\u201d \u201cOk, but what if the Solar is also a thaumaturge?\u201d I mean, that\u2019s why we had charms that were perfect unless someone spent wp to resist and then they just splintered. Which ...I dunno, didn\u2019t really feel right to me.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... Would you be angry if the Fae normally defaulted to DB power levels, but could ascend to Celestial power levels by feeding on humans? Would that feel like Fae working as intended and giving incentives to be a soul sucking predator? Or would it feel like the game was punishing you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T03:12:08-07:00","id":1306214,"title":"","content":"I don't think Fae need to change too much, a lot of their thematic was undercut not by actually being underpowered, but because the direction of 2ed was Perfect effects and Total counters.<br /> <br /> That said I feel like the simplest solution is just for every Raksha to be a power level unto themselves. Assume that most of the ones you encounter are somewhat more capable than mortals, that some have DB level effects and some have Celestial level.<br /> <br /> The main ways to differentiate these effects are by theme and charm caps, which are a)Wildly different for Raksha in any case and b) Easily approximate from the existing books.<br /> <br /> Assuming they had a whole charm set to themselves, I think (As was found in 2nd ed) it'd be hard to represent the same character creation accounting for Dace's rival Cataphract, Hand-dress lady, clam baby, Lion piper, freaking Balor, AND the chump Lilith calls out within one second of encountering him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T07:40:23-07:00","id":1306250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1306191#post1306191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say that I think Raksha, from the way they are portrayed in the fiction, should be hella scary to everyone. Including Solar exalted.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, not even the likes of Spear-Empress Bhadri should just be able to win forever against everyone.<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m not sure where the balance point is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Age and experience.<br /> <br /> You need to establish two power-levels: The PC starting floor level, and the ceiling where a PC's power should stop.<br /> <br /> Another thing you need to establish is how MANY Raksha there are, and how likely you are to find multiple Raksha together.<br /> <br /> There are vastly more Terrestrial Exalted than Celestial Exalted, and the Terrestrial Exaltation's hereditary nature means you're almost always going to encounter multiple Terrestrials together, and they're very likely to have built a power-base to assist them.<br /> <br /> Raksha should likewise outnumber Celestial Exalted. But do they outnumber even the Terrestrial Exalted?<br /> <br /> How often do Raksha produce other Raksha, to grow or maintain their numbers in the face of natural attrition? Essentially, do Raksha naturally form groups by having children?<br /> <br /> Do Raksha naturally form groups for reasons other than making children? Or are they generally more concerned with having as much control of their surroundings as possible, than sticking together for self-defense?<br /> <br /> If Raksha are more numerous than Terrestrial Exalted, and generally living far away from the various Terrestrial Empires, how often do Raksha NEED to band together for self-defense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T09:10:36-07:00","id":1306261,"title":"","content":"Should a PC be able to become Adeimantus or Spear-Empress Bhadri then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T10:21:28-07:00","id":1306278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1306191#post1306191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... Would you be angry if the Fae normally defaulted to DB power levels, but could ascend to Celestial power levels by feeding on humans? Would that feel like Fae working as intended and giving incentives to be a soul sucking predator? Or would it feel like the game was punishing you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they need a two-tier system. The main thing Fair Folk have going for them over most Exalts is that it's pretty easy to introduce a powerful noble that you've never heard of as an outside context problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T11:18:58-07:00","id":1306287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1306214#post1306214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming they had a whole charm set to themselves, I think (As was found in 2nd ed) it'd be hard to represent the same character creation accounting for Dace's rival Cataphract, Hand-dress lady, clam baby, Lion piper, freaking Balor, AND the chump Lilith calls out within one second of encountering him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind, those might all be different categories of being. The first two are nobles, the second two could be commoners, the fellow with Lilith was the Emanation of an Unshaped (who was also trying to pass himself off as a Solar of all things), and Balor is basically a Fair Folk Incarna.<br /> <br /> It leaves me with the question of how one differs between commoners and nobles. The process from the prior Editions was fairly limited, but it also seems that giving them very different paths threatens to overcomplicate it.<br /> <br /> I think the matter of nobles having personalized imagery and distinct panoplies might help with that; not merely in the idea that they have access to Evocations or something, but that there might be something like a... well, like things with Aura, or the Protean and Mastery keywords, now that I think of it. Base Charms that then have an added something when used by a noble, that evinces their particular style. I'm not sure if that would be best done more freeform, with powers that have empty slots in which to fit the noble's process, or unlocking condition depending on the noble's broad type that might end up with an eclectic mix.<br /> <br /> Yes, Martial Arts and Evocations do display a certain capacity to give a particular Charm cascade internal variations in power level.<br /> <br /> That and it would help to not have huge chunks of their Charms only useful for shaping combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T12:14:06-07:00","id":1306299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1306261#post1306261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should a PC be able to become Adeimantus or Spear-Empress Bhadri then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Should a Solar PC be able to become Queen Merela, or Desus, or Eternal Nova the Sword-Saint?<br /> <br /> The only kind of characters that PCs shouldn't get support for becoming are Yozis and Metropoli.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T12:28:14-07:00","id":1306301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1306250#post1306250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raksha should likewise outnumber Celestial Exalted. But do they outnumber even the Terrestrial Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that commoners should outnumber Dragon Blooded significantly, while still not being much in the face of the world's mortal populations, and that nobles should outnumber the Exalted slightly, but have issues with restricted conditions for operating in Creation and a tendency to be bad at cooperating with one another.<br /> <br /> Part of that would be their egos, part would just be an emergent property of building themselves out of impulses that are probably often irreconcilable.<br /> <br /> Most nobles have retinues of commoners, but most commoners are functioning independently, often gathered into little groups of their own; it's easier for them to get along, as they find one another's proclivities complementary and inviting, in addition to it being good for survival.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about the intricacies of gossamer, but I'm attracted to the idea that even some of the most impoverished nobles have wealth in Creation's milieu that would confound the majority of Dynasts (although there are obstacles to effectively transitioning it to Creation). Hence, when you're a lone noble below the stage where you're an existential terror in your own right, you can probably stand out with some effective pomp.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How often do Raksha produce other Raksha, to grow or maintain their numbers in the face of natural attrition? Essentially, do Raksha naturally form groups by having children?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I like the general idea that the Raksha have a limited capacity to produce more of themselves, especially under the circumstances they find themselves in. <br /> <br /> I'm also picturing an idea that many Raksha that could produce more don't, because they're already competing for limited resources. They don't suffer from natural population loss, but it also means that many of the circumstances in which producing more would be really helpful are going to be a lot harder, because... you've lost most of the ones that could shape somebody. So populations that experience major disaster can crash hard.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T13:22:54-07:00","id":1306323,"title":"","content":"Commoners aren\u2019t Raksha; they\u2019re Wyld creatures enslaved by Raksha.<br /> <br /> Raksha are the PC splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T13:25:58-07:00","id":1306324,"title":"","content":"The lorelai and cataphract in the core read to me as separated from the likes of Adeimantus by more than Essence.<br /> <br /> Similar goes with the Directional trends given to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T13:47:54-07:00","id":1306333,"title":"","content":"yeah their mentioned to serve Nobles, making it sound like they aren't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T15:47:06-07:00","id":1306349,"title":"","content":"Following my point about less powerful nobles still having retinues and income of some resource (which I'll refer to as gossamer for convenience), I had a notion that the time since the Balorian Crusade has represented a shift in their dynamics.<br /> <br /> Prior to that, the Raksha being more numerous, having virtually unrestricted access across the Wyld, and being at the top of the food chain, meant that even the least of the nobility had access to vast quantities of gossamer, by which they surrounded themselves with grand quantities of unimaginable wonders and maintained authority over large numbers of commoners and innumerable lesser creatures. Their monopoly on this resource kept the lesser Raksha bound in service, dependent on rewards for good service (often in fierce competition with one another) and the whims of their masters. Even such a minor noble could launch raids into Creation to reap hundreds or thousands of souls in a single swoop, with which to make up for any deficits. The greatest of the nobles had power and authority and resources sufficient to launch the great breakthroughs that could devastate major cities, and several managing to act in concert could set large portions of a whole Direction in disarray.<br /> <br /> Since the failure of the Crusade, they've fallen severely. The hannya nipping at their heels have largely cut them off from the vast dream resources of the Wyld, and they're forced to scavenge at the edges of Creation. There would have always been the types to present themselves more magnanimously, but in the current era a greater number are obligated to do so with something closer to sincerity out of need (a fact that the Guild managed to recognise and has profited greatly from capitalising upon; they know that cutting off vital supplies can give them an edge). The least nobles have so little (some of it derived even from stipends jealously doled out by those above them), that often their retinues of commoners are employed on a provisional basis.<br /> <br /> What's more, the commoners outnumber them significantly. Not in a manner that might overwhelm and overthrow their superiors (the nature of their complementary powers makes it difficult for them to enact violence, or even avoid falling into a subservient role), but that puts many of them outside of that reach. For the first time in their existence (which even for commoners can have been a very long time), a lot of them are functioning independently. They often band together for safety and greater strength for acting against mortals, and where they might need what nobles provide, they can often have higher negotiating power. This often leads to offering competitive mercenary rates (or ruthlessly eliminating competition in order to gouge their prices), but some have discovered the values of collective bargaining. That's another project of the Guild; there's a contingent within them that sees value in keeping the prices of the more independent commoners high, as that puts more nobles under pressure to convert greater quantities of dreams to gossamer, putting them increasingly in the pocket of Guild slave traders.<br /> <br /> And with that greater independence, you get more commoners becoming stronger than they would have under the dominion of nobles. Perhaps there's a possibility that they might develop into a new kind of power.<br /> <br /> What do people think? Too Changeling: the Dreaming?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T16:20:48-07:00","id":1306357,"title":"","content":"If gossamer is a resource like motes or Willpower points, how should Raksha generate it?<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind the very important detail that motes and Willpower are limited by an individual\u2019s capacity for both, and no one can simply stockpile more over time.<br /> <br /> So alternatively, gossamer might be a magical material used like metal or cloth, rather than fuel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T17:32:07-07:00","id":1306367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1306357#post1306357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If gossamer is a resource like motes or Willpower points, how should Raksha generate it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in the prior Editions, it was reaped from waypoints by shaping actions as well as being an additional product when they used Feeding Charms on mortals.<br /> <br /> The amount of gossamer that was supposed to be available from any given waypoint was somewhat arbitrary, and said to be a function of how much Fair Folk activity had taken place there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping in mind the very important detail that motes and Willpower are limited by an individual\u2019s capacity for both, and no one can simply stockpile more over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gossamer was in a curious place in which it was a numerically counter resource akin to those stats, and even spent on Charms, but was supposed to be something technically separate from (if attuned to) a given Raksha, and that they could store Elsewhere in technically limitless quantity.<br /> <br /> I'll note that, as far as I could ever tell, Graceful Wicked Masques was always a lot more vague about what gossamer was and where it came from. I've recently found Exalted: the Fair Folk to not only be much more clear about how it's acquired from waypoints, but even gives it visible attributes.<br /> <br /> I'm torn on gossamer. On the one hand, I see it as an element of Fair Folk mechanics that adds to their overcomplication of the base system, in addition to having some issues with how the potential to stockpile it could mess with some Charms that it paid for; those seem like compelling arguments to be rid of it. On the other, I'm greatly moved by the premises of a dream material that functions as a resource for the Raksha, that is readily converted into disproportionately large wealth in Creation, but whose true value in how it drives their social economy derives from the manner in which it feeds Raksha existence.<br /> <br /> It's somewhat akin to Yu-Shan's ambrosia, but I feel as though the dynamic was very different; ambrosia merely serves to fuel divine luxury, where gossamer was laid out as something necessary to their well-being.<br /> <br /> It might get by without being made specifically numerical, but I also feel as though that interacts awkwardly with the premise that it's reaped by Feeding on mortals.<br /> <br /> I think it will probably be removed, and I'm open to that. I would hope that the personal and social dynamics underlying it would be retained, but I'm not sure of how. I would feel the loss of those things from the Fair Folk.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T18:14:03-07:00","id":1306374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1306367#post1306367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's somewhat akin to Yu-Shan's ambrosia, but I feel as though the dynamic was very different; ambrosia merely serves to fuel divine luxury, where gossamer was laid out as something necessary to their well-being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, gods and Sidereals can't spend ambrosia in place of motes, Willpower points, health levels, Initiative, or anything else they might need to spend on Charms.<br /> <br /> Ambrosia is a material resource not unlike firedust or a magical material. You can spend firedust to discharge a flame weapon, but anyone can do that, and it's ultimately no different from arrows or other forms of ammunition. You can use starmetal to forge artifacts, but raw starmetal does you no good in battle, you can only have so many artifacts attuned at once, and you have limited time too make starmetal artifacts or discover their Evocations.<br /> <br /> Motes, Willpower points, health levels, and Initiative pools are all intensely personal resources with strict restrictions against stockpiling them ahead of time in preparation for battle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it will probably be removed, and I'm open to that. I would hope that the personal and social dynamics underlying it would be retained, but I'm not sure of how. I would feel the loss of those things from the Fair Folk. </div> </div> </div>The base system already has rules for hunger and deprivation. Gossamer could be treated as food (or water) for Raksha; something they need to live, rather than something they use to fuel their powers. That preserves the narrative without impacting game balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T18:52:06-07:00","id":1306386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1306374#post1306374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, gods and Sidereals can't spend ambrosia in place of motes, Willpower points, health levels, Initiative, or anything else they might need to spend on Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a derivation of my point about necessity for Raksha well-being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ambrosia is a material resource not unlike firedust or a magical material. You can spend firedust to discharge a flame weapon, but anyone can do that, and it's ultimately no different from arrows or other forms of ammunition. You can use starmetal to forge artifacts, but raw starmetal does you no good in battle, you can only have so many artifacts attuned at once, and you have limited time too make starmetal artifacts or discover their Evocations.<br /> <br /> Motes, Willpower points, health levels, and Initiative pools are all intensely personal resources with strict restrictions against stockpiling them ahead of time in preparation for battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... know all of this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The base system already has rules for hunger and deprivation. Gossamer could be treated as food (or water) for Raksha; something they need to live, rather than something they use to fuel their powers. That preserves the narrative without impacting game balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rendering gossamer as literal food would not be satisfying to me. It lacks the direct connotations of their systems of value, and makes their driving impulses feel overtly crude. It also feels to me like something that doesn't quite have sufficient weight, although I couldn't say how seriously people take the notion that their characters might starve to death.<br /> <br /> Hmm, that's illustrating to me some of the possible weaknesses in calcification rules, but that's a separate discussion.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think... there's a Resources Merit that connotes a source of income, as well as the implication of having wealth to spend to accomplish things in the setting, without that being valued numerically. There's a description of ways to utilise the travails of fluctuating wealth as a source of stories, which could transplant in basic principles to descriptions of the Raksha and a theoretical Gossamer Merit; how for them, gossamer is primarily spent as a token of status between Raksha and a means to luxuriate in splendour, as well as a raw material for constructive efforts that can't be substituted, and the storyline means of accumulating it are different and have different dynamics, while still being largely abstracted. Maybe some Charms that don't use it in the manner of motes to fuel, but still reference ratings in the Merit?<br /> <br /> I don't know; it's hard to get over the idea that it has some use in Charms, because I feel as though Raksha live in the use of their powers more than the Exalted would. I keep trying to imagine gossamer having the same value as sources of wealth would for a Dynast character, but something about it doesn't feel right. It makes the Raksha feel too materialistic, when the things that I value about gossamer are it being a currency of status and experiences.<br /> <br /> But maybe that attachment to Charms is my enemy here. Maybe things would be simpler if there was dedicated description of the meaning of gossamer's value is to the Raksha, and the only power that needs to reference it are one or more concerns with manufacturing that state that they require a source of gossamer that can take the form of the Merit or roleplaying access to a source, such as a patron or brief access to a deposit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T20:39:24-07:00","id":1306406,"title":"","content":"My pet Theory re: fair folk, and one that I\u2019ll use if I ever run a game that focuses on the Wyld, is that the Hannya have been more present since Balorian Crusade because Hannya are simply manifestations of the Raksha\u2019s fears.<br /> <br /> Not pretend fears. Real actual terror at the prospect of petrification and nonexistence. That what is driving the Raksha into Creation now is expressions of their idea of the Realm Defense Grid. Enormous and invisible beasts spouting bursts of fury that render everything their path into inanimate crystal.<br /> <br /> The practical solution then, if you want the easier path of Raksha being able to safely remain in the wyld and not bother Creation, is to somehow trick or convince the majority of them into not being scared of the grid, or thinking it\u2019s completely inoperable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T04:52:40-07:00","id":1306506,"title":"","content":"Personally I wasn\u2019t too fond of the Hannya in 2nd edition and much preferred 1st editions take on the Fair Folk. I think the Unshaped were reason enough for the Shaped to remain in Creation and only quest through the Wyld in search of power, Gossamer or to alleviate boredom and the very existence of Creation was enough for the Unshaped to hate it and seek it\u2019s destruction.<br /> <br /> The addition of a new undefined threath from the Wyld that drives the Fair Folk to seek shape and to escape into Creation was unnecessary and kinda boring in my personal opinion. But as always YMMV.<br /> <br /> Gossamer is a kinda tricky subject. I kinda liked it during the 1st edition but hoarding it was a problem that continued in the 2nd edition. Still I like the idea of even the most destitute Fae being wealthy in Creation as their Dream currency is formed from potential to actual. Also Gossamer has been integral part of their Charms since the beginning so it is difficult to seperate the two now. It is thematically cool and awesome that you pay with Gossamer on effects where you create something from your Wyld energy into creation proper but balancing it is quite difficult. So either there has to be a cap for Gossamer or Gossamer costs should not be used for balancing a Charm but more to give it thematic weigh and to drive in the point that it\u2019s functions can truly affect creation as more than mere illusions. Balancing Charms should be done with mote and wp cost as normal.<br /> <br /> As a side note, as big fan of 1st edition that I am (transitioned to 2nd only after Infernals), I did like Holdens errata on Fair Folk for 2nd edition. He gave them a lot of fun Charms for In Creation use. Also what should be learned from that errata is that each Charm given to Fair Folk should have utility and function both in Creation and in the Wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T10:48:25-07:00","id":1306572,"title":"","content":"Echo Charms were a crude stop gap to redeem how much of the Fair Folk Charms were dedicated to shaping combat. Building something from the ground up in which the complexity of shaping combat has been divested doesn't need it, and finding other unique things for Charms to do in the Wyld that wouldn't be perfectly functional in Creation (or can be dedicated specifically to the Wyld) sounds awfully unwieldy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:56:10-07:00","id":1306600,"title":"","content":"Good riddance to shaping combat, and the people who wrote the Echo Charmset should have been paid for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T09:58:01-07:00","id":1306877,"title":"","content":"If shaping combat is going to be entirely left out then we truly need Fair Folk Charms that allow them to loose a combat and \u201ddie\u201d so elegantly and beatufully as for you to weep for them and in so doing create a tie of love or respect to them that stays in place even after they re-create themselves from their death and other such cool things originally left to shaping combat. <br /> <br /> Shaping combat was perhaps a bit complicated but still quite awesome in the freedom it gave and the epic combats it allowed for which were often on scale unprecedented even in Exalted. I think it serves a purpose but I do understand those of you who wish to get rid of it as it was a completely seperate system. Perhaps if it could somehow be more integrated into the already somewhat more cinematic combat of 3rd ed it could againbe something awesome.<br /> <br /> But that is just a personal opinion of mine. <br /> <br /> I do however 100% agree that Holden should have been paid for the awesome errata he wrote for the Geaceful Wicked Masques.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:01:03-07:00","id":1306990,"title":"","content":"I think just allowing for more flexibility with the Wyld Stunt/System could accomplish this.<br /> <br /> Yeah, you &quot;die&quot;, but you aren't dead when you have your tear-jerking soliloquy on your death bed. Next scene you just spend an action shaping away your death and go about your life.<br /> <br /> So no extra shaping tracks or that jazz, just regular character sheet conditions, but you can just make a fantasy roll and shape them away, kinda like how you could just change your intimacies willy nilly. Just because your little body you shaped for yourself has 7 levels of lethal, doesn't mean that you're dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T15:20:55-07:00","id":1307003,"title":"","content":"There were always some interesting ideas attached to shaping combat, but I think something was lost in the fact that basically all of them were just stunts, and the books were never exactly the best at describing them.<br /> <br /> I feel as though it might be worthwhile to take those ideas and make them the actual forms that various kinds of illusory powers take. It's less freeform, but I think it would play better with the game's usual attitudes.<br /> <br /> I think that some of the shaping combat consequences could be systemized in alternative ways, or else encouraged with compelling descriptions of how the Fair Folk are liable to react to certain scenarios. Say, their sensibilities are likely to be very melodramatic even in cases where a person actually did die in a manner that they perceived to be beautiful, and a power to create an illusory death merely capitalises upon that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:24:47-07:00","id":1307035,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve honestly been wondering if doing some kind of Mage the Awakening type freeform magic system would fit best for the Fae, but getting that to work in Exalted could be trickier than usual and balance would be extra difficult.<br /> <br /> Some kind of hybrid setup where they can access charms they haven\u2019t purchased for an increased cost might work better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:33:38-07:00","id":1307041,"title":"","content":"Another point to think about is \u201cwhen should a Raksha\u2019s powers be illusions you can ignore and when should they be \u201creal?\u201d And should there be any kind of middle ground between those two states?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:51:12-07:00","id":1307051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1307041#post1307041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another point to think about is \u201cwhen should a Raksha\u2019s powers be illusions you can ignore and when should they be \u201creal?\u201d And should there be any kind of middle ground between those two states?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though I can see the point being made about a distinction of how much Fair Folk powers count when directed at things in Creation, but feel as though it came at the expense of their credibility and functionality.<br /> <br /> I can't recall what if anything I've said about the subject in the past, but right now I feel as though giving Fair Folk a lot of free reign with what they do to their Intimacies is a lot more of an issue, because Intimacies have a lot more significance here than they did in Second Edition. That and how they model things that even by that Edition's standards might be presumed to remain consist in one's identity.<br /> <br /> I think something could capture the spirit of the idea while being adapted to this system in a power resembling what Adeimantus can do to force people to introduce facts about his city, that he can gain Minor Principles corresponding to (and something to do with being a bit stronger when acting in line with them?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T04:46:22-07:00","id":1308459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1306278#post1306278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they need a two-tier system. The main thing Fair Folk have going for them over most Exalts is that it's pretty easy to introduce a powerful noble that you've never heard of as an outside context problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Expanding on this. The main thing that weakens Dragon-Blooded is their dramatis personae.<br /> <br /> If an essence 6 Dragon-Blooded shows up in your game you owe your players something of an explanation as to why they're significantly more powerful than the luminaries of the Scarlet Dynasty.<br /> With Fair Folk I think there should be a decent sized negative space where that kind of character can already exist.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T11:06:51-07:00","id":1308489,"title":"","content":"That seems like a true point, but less so for characters that aren't politically prominent... Are players really going to worry about why a Ragara Myrrun type (should he appear and *not* promptly explode), not really involved in politics, just very cultivated in essence, might be Essence 6?<br /> <br /> Plus to some extent, you can relax it in a given game by upping the essence scores of the Realm NPCs should they appear in your game - the designers tend to be fairly explicit that statblocs are just a guideline after all (going back to GCG saying that if Ahlat seems like a pushover, whatever, just load him up with perfect defenses and whatever you need to strengthen him).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T11:37:30-07:00","id":1308496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1308489#post1308489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like a true point, but less so for characters that aren't politically prominent... Are players really going to worry about why a Ragara Myrrun type (should he appear and *not* promptly explode), not really involved in politics, just very cultivated in essence, might be Essence 6?</div> </div> </div> </div>He might not be involved in politics, but he might still be involved in the kinds of things that have him encountering the PCs. I'm also not really sure if the milieu of Exalted lends itself to a character having attained such Essence while being cloistered off.<br /> <br /> That said, the matter of Dragon Blooded being weakened by lack of Exalted above Essence 5 begs the question of why that should be a significant addition, considering the more low-key approach to such Essence levels this time around.<br /> <br /> Which leads back to the question of if it should mean the same thing for Fair Folk as it does for Exalted. I can see issues with either approach.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T09:19:38-07:00","id":1308697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1307041#post1307041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another point to think about is \u201cwhen should a Raksha\u2019s powers be illusions you can ignore and when should they be \u201creal?\u201d And should there be any kind of middle ground between those two states?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think they should have two distinct avenues of power, making illusions and making stuff, and the fact that the populace at large doesn't always know the distinction leads to the misconception of their powers.<br /> <br /> A sliding scale of realness for a certain power would be a really difficult needle to thread, if it could, otherwise you end up with the problems we already had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:36:32-07:00","id":1308744,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I suppose the issue with Raksha having \u201cIllusion\u201d as one of the big factors in their powerset is the one that comes up when you imagine the classic story of \u201cTraveler takes shelter in wondrous castle for the night, wakes up in an abandoned hovel.\u201d And that is, what happens when you try to consider the logistics/consequences?<br /> <br /> Did any of the food that guy ate last night even exist? Would the roof have kept out the wind and rain? Was there some way the guy could have seen through the illusion? Could the traveler have climbed up on the parapet and looked around? Basically, how does all this interact with each other?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you view the Fae as \u201creality-warpers,\u201d who can just call up chunks of matter or reshape reality on a whim, those questions become easy to answer since it\u2019s all \u201creal.\u201d On the other hand, now you need to figure out some new limits to put on the Fae. My knee jerk reaction is that, outside of the Wyld, their reality shaping tends to cost more and not last very long. Also it likely needs to conform to your identity.<br /> <br /> For example, see how Adeimantus can just summon forth a chunk of architecture from his \u201cIdeal City\u201d to provide cover for himself, but it goes away quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T17:33:24-07:00","id":1308839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1308489#post1308489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are players really going to worry about why a Ragara Myrrun type (should he appear and *not* promptly explode), not really involved in politics, just very cultivated in essence, might be Essence 6?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sense that if you don't offer a sufficient textual explaination it's going to fall to the the metatextual reason &quot;I wanted my original character to be one of the most powerful people in the world&quot; which isn't necessarily bad if your PCs are a circle of essence 5 Solars desperate for a challenge but there are players who can and do see it as a red flag.<br /> <br /> It's not a unique problem for Dragon-Blooded but in comparison Lunars have more essence 6+ exalts and Bear's Sleep Technique can be used to create the kind of negative space I'm talking about. I just talked about Dragon-Blooded because people in this thread have been infering they don't consider Dragon-Blooded power level sufficient for the strongest of the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1303383-what-are-iconic-fae-powers?p=1308496#post1308496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the matter of Dragon Blooded being weakened by lack of Exalted above Essence 5 begs the question of why that should be a significant addition, considering the more low-key approach to such Essence levels this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its a very meaningful choice in an NPC's design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-29-2019, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}